From e85a8e53c3ec862cc860000883c330a1a76d0716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:13:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] dt-bindings: pwm: add hi3798mv100 pwm

The Hi3798MV100 carries the PMOC block too: its three outputs sit at the
same offsets and feed the core, CPU and GPU rails of that SoC. The
output count is what each SoC contributes to the block, so give the
MV100 its own compatible value.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/pwm/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm.yaml | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pwm/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pwm/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm.yaml
@@ -14,14 +14,17 @@ description:
   SoC provides three PWM outputs, which on the reference designs drive the
   feedback node of an external converter such as a pwm-regulator. The number
   of outputs differs between the SoCs carrying this block, so each SoC has
-  its own compatible value.
+  its own compatible value. The Hi3798MV100 carries the same block, whose
+  three outputs sit at the same offsets and feed its core, CPU and GPU rails.
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: pwm.yaml#
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm
+    enum:
+      - hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm
+      - hisilicon,hi3798mv100-pwm
 
   reg:
     description:
